{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.BlochGroupQuotientConstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.BlochGroupQuotientConstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.QuotientGroup.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeAbelianGroup","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers"],"declarations":33,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.quot_rogersGenerator_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.quot_rogersGenerator_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L345-L362","doc":"**Rogers pentagon vanishes in the Bloch quotient.** Every\nRogers-form pentagon generator maps to zero under the\ncanonical projection `quot`. This is the defining property\nof the Bloch group: the 5-term Rogers identity holds.\n\nWith the constrained generator set (post-#575 swap-in), this\ntheorem replaces the previous `quot_pentagonGenerator_eq_zero`\nover arbitrary `PentagonShape F` (which would no longer\nbe provable, since arbitrary 5-tuples are no longer in the\npentagon subgroup). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.rogersGenerator_mem_pentagonSubgroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.rogersGenerator_mem_pentagonSubgroup","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L333-L343","doc":"**Rogers-generator membership lemma.** Every Rogers-form\npentagon generator lies inside the pentagon `AddSubgroup`\n(the closure of `validPentagonRelationGenerators` contains\nits generators by construction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.quot_universal_property","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.quot_universal_property","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L312-L331","doc":"**Universal property of the quotient.** Any additive group\nhomomorphism `f : PreBlochGroup F →+ G` that sends every\npentagon-relation generator to zero factors uniquely through\n`quot`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.quot_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.quot_add","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L307-L310","doc":"Sums map through `quot` additively. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.quot_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.quot_zero","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L302-L305","doc":"The zero of `BlochGroup F` is the image of zero under\n`quot`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.quot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.quot","kind":"def","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L298-L300","doc":"The **canonical projection** `PreBlochGroup F → BlochGroup F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.instAddCommGroupBlochGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.instAddCommGroupBlochGroup","kind":"instance","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L293-L296","doc":"`BlochGroup F` carries the `AddCommGroup` structure inherited\nfrom the quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.BlochGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.BlochGroup","kind":"def","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L280-L291","doc":"**The Bloch group as a quotient.**\n\n`BlochGroup F := PreBlochGroup F ⧸ pentagonSubgroup`.\n\nThis is an `AddCommGroup` by Mathlib's `QuotientAddGroup`\nconstruction. The canonical projection\n`mk : PreBlochGroup F → BlochGroup F` is an additive group\nhomomorphism. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:bloch-group-quotient-construction","label":"prop:bloch-group-quotient-construction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.pentagonSubgroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.pentagonSubgroup","kind":"def","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L263-L278","doc":"The **pentagon `AddSubgroup`** of `PreBlochGroup F`,\ngenerated by the **constrained Rogers-form** pentagon\nrelation set. This is the kernel we quotient by. Using\nMathlib's `AddSubgroup.closure`.\n\n**Switched (post-#574 follow-up).** Previously this subgroup\nwas generated by the unconstrained `pentagonRelationGenerators`\n(over arbitrary 5-tuples in `PentagonShape`), which collapsed\nthe quotient on degenerate shapes. With the full 5-element\n`rogersGenerator` constructor in place\n(`RogersPair.shape₃/₄/₅`, sorry-free), the constrained\n`validPentagonRelationGenerators` is now the active generator\nset — fixing the over-permissive-quotient bug structurally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.pentagonRelationGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.pentagonRelationGenerators","kind":"def","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L245-L261","doc":"The set of **(unconstrained) pentagon relation generators** in\n`PreBlochGroup F` — the image of `pentagonGenerator` over all\narbitrary 5-tuples of pre-Bloch elements. This set is\nover-permissive (degenerate shapes collapse to single\n`of(eᵢ)` elements; see `PentagonShape` doc).\n\n**No longer the active generator set.** As of PR #575,\n`pentagonSubgroup` is generated by the constrained Rogers-form\nset `validPentagonRelationGenerators` (using the full\n5-element `rogersGenerator`). This unconstrained set is\nretained as the structural skeleton parametrising pentagon\nshapes for arbitrary types `F`; downstream callers that need\nthe proper Bloch group should use `validPentagonRelationGenerators`\ndirectly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.validPentagonRelationGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.validPentagonRelationGenerators","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L232-L243","doc":"The **constrained pentagon-relation generators** for a `Field F`:\nimage of the full 5-element `rogersGenerator` over all valid\nRogers pairs. Restricts to **shape-parameter-derived** relation\nelements rather than arbitrary 5-tuples — the proper direction\nfor the Bloch-group quotient. With this, the\nover-permissiveness flagged in PR #574 review is fixed\nstructurally for any `Field F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.rogersGenerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.rogersGenerator","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L216-L230","doc":"The **full 5-element Rogers pentagon-relation generator** at a\nvalid Rogers pair, using all five shape parameters\n`(x, y, y/x, (1-y⁻¹)/(1-x⁻¹), (1-y)/(1-x))` with explicit\n`PreBlochElement` constructors. The standard 5-term Rogers\nidentity asserts this combination vanishes in the Bloch\ngroup. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.rogersGeneratorPartial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.rogersGeneratorPartial","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L202-L214","doc":"The pentagon-relation generator at a Rogers pair, using only\nits `e₁ = x`, `e₂ = y`, `e₃ = y/x` shape parameters and\nderived domain-validity proofs. The full 5-tuple version\n`pentagonShapeOfRogersPair` requires the additional `e₄, e₅`\nproofs which expand similarly. We provide the partial three-\nparameter version here as a structural building block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.shape₅","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.shape₅","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L179-L200","doc":"The fifth derived shape parameter `(1 - y)/(1 - x)`:\nwell-defined and `≠ 0, ≠ 1` from the Rogers conditions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.shape₄","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.shape₄","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L148-L177","doc":"The fourth derived shape parameter `(1 - y⁻¹)/(1 - x⁻¹)`:\nwell-defined and `≠ 0, ≠ 1` from the Rogers conditions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.shape₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.shape₃","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L103-L119","doc":"The first derived shape parameter `y/x`: well-defined and\n`≠ 0, ≠ 1` from the Rogers conditions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.hxy_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.hxy_ne","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.hy_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.hy_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.hy_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.hy_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.hx_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.hx_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.hx_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.hx_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.y","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.x","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.x","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair.mk","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.RogersPair","kind":"structure","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L87-L101","doc":"A **valid Rogers pair** `(x, y) ∈ F × F` satisfying the\npentagon-domain constraints needed for all five derived shape\nparameters to lie in `F \\ {0, 1}`. The basic conditions\n`x, y ∈ F \\ {0, 1}` and `x ≠ y` together imply that the\nderived parameters `y/x, (1-y⁻¹)/(1-x⁻¹), (1-y)/(1-x)` are\nall in `F \\ {0, 1}` for any `Field F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.pentagonGenerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.pentagonGenerator","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L71-L85","doc":"The **pentagon-relation generator** at a given shape is the\nformal alternating sum of its five pre-Bloch elements:\n\n  e₁ - e₂ + e₃ - e₄ + e₅\n\nin the free abelian group. The standard Rogers-form 5-term\nidentity asserts this combination vanishes in the Bloch\ngroup. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.e₅","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.e₅","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.e₄","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.e₄","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.e₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.e₃","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.e₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.e₂","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.e₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.e₁","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochQuotient.PentagonShape","kind":"structure","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bloch-group-quotient-construction.lean#L47-L69","doc":"A **pentagon shape** is intended to be a quintuple of pre-Bloch\nelements derived from a pair `(x, y) ∈ (F \\ {0,1})²` via the\n5-term Rogers-form maps `x, y, y/x, (1-y⁻¹)/(1-x⁻¹), (1-y)/(1-x)`.\n\n**Caveat (over-permissive).** As declared, this structure\nallows ARBITRARY 5-tuples of pre-Bloch elements, not the\nconstrained Rogers-form 5-tuples. Any concrete instance with\nrepeated entries (e.g. `e₂ = e₃ = e₄ = e₅`) yields a\npentagon-relation generator that collapses to `of(e₁)`,\nputting individual pre-Bloch elements into the relation\nsubgroup and trivialising the quotient. The proper fix is a\n`ValidPentagonShape F` predicate enforcing the Rogers-form\nconstraints (deferred to a future commit alongside\n`Field F` arithmetic for the inverse and division maps).\nThe structural skeleton below supports this drop-in\nrefinement without modification. ","signatureChunk":0}]}